---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Product management is applied philosophy — Greg O\'Brien" current={2}>
<div data-screen-label="Note">
<div style="border-top:1px solid var(--edge);margin-top:38px;padding:40px 56px 0">
<a href="/think" style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);text-decoration:none;transition:color .2s ease" class="h-ink">← All notes</a>
</div>
<div style="padding:34px 56px 44px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule)">
<div style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;color:var(--muted)">Jun 2026</div>
<h1 style="margin:18px 0 0;font-family:Newsreader,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:54px;line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.02em;max-width:22ch">Product management is applied <span style="font-style:italic">philosophy</span></h1>
<p style="margin:18px 0 0;font-size:16px;line-height:1.65;max-width:46ch;color:var(--body)">Roadmaps are really just values written down and defended in public. The job is philosophy with a deadline.</p>
</div>
<div style="padding:40px 56px 24px"><div style="border:1px solid var(--edge)"><div data-shot="1" style="aspect-ratio:16/9;background:var(--stripe);display:flex;align-items:flex-end;padding:20px"><span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.08em;color:var(--muted)">[ AGENT PHOTO ]</span></div></div></div>
<div style="padding:0 56px 44px;max-width:70ch">
<p style="margin:0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--body)">Every roadmap is a values statement, whether anyone admits it or not. Deciding what a team builds next is deciding what matters most right now, and defending that decision out loud, in a room, to people who disagree with you.</p>
<p style="margin:22px 0 0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--body)">I studied philosophy before I did anything resembling product work, and for a long time I thought that was an odd detour. It wasn’t. Prioritization is ethics with a deadline — you’re constantly trading one good thing for another good thing and having to explain why.</p>
<div style="margin-top:34px;font-size:17px;font-weight:600">Where the philosophy actually shows up</div>
<p style="margin:9px 0 0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--body)">Not in the vocabulary — nobody wants to hear about a philosopher’s name in a planning meeting, and if you need one to make your point, you haven’t found the plain version of it yet. It shows up in the questions: whose problem are we actually solving, what are we quietly deciding not to fix, and are we being honest with ourselves about why.</p>
<div style="margin-top:34px;font-family:Newsreader,serif;font-size:25px;line-height:1.25;max-width:52ch">"A roadmap is just a values statement that hasn’t been caught yet."</div>
<p style="margin:34px 0 0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--body)">The best product leaders I’ve worked with aren’t the ones with the cleanest frameworks. They’re the ones willing to say, out loud, “this is a values call, not a data call” — and then make it anyway, because someone has to.</p>
<div style="margin-top:26px;border:1px dashed var(--dash)"><div data-shot="1" style="height:190px;background:var(--stripe);display:flex;align-items:flex-end;padding:20px"><span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;color:var(--muted);letter-spacing:.08em">[ OPTIONAL DIAGRAM ]</span></div></div>
<div style="margin-top:34px;font-size:17px;font-weight:600">The nugget</div>
<p style="margin:9px 0 0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--body)">Next time you’re stuck prioritizing, stop asking what’s most valuable and start asking what you actually believe matters. The prioritization usually follows.</p>
</div>
<div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:40px 56px 14px;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline">
<span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted)">Next note</span>
<a href="/think" style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);text-decoration:none;transition:color .2s ease" class="h-ink">All notes →</a>
</div>
<div style="padding:14px 56px 44px;max-width:70ch">
<a href="/think/why-agent-is-doing-too-much-work-as-a-word" style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;gap:20px;padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--ruleSoft);text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);transition:color .2s ease" class="h-accent"><span style="font-family:Newsreader,serif;font-size:23px;line-height:1.3">Why "agent" is doing too much work as a word</span><span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;color:var(--muted);white-space:nowrap">Aug 2026</span></a>
</div>
</div>
</Layout>
